  "body": "## Scope\nIndependent, source-aware LRS Bianchi-I **conditional positive H/He photo-reaction** reference, stacked on PR #149 commit `d5246c500522ffe4efe904f3206a60f9541c7dbd`. Does **not** change PR #150 FLRW production, other branches, checkpoint/source configurations, or running NCP q512/q1024 full-history campaign.\n\n## Constructive physics and implementation\n- Exact positive paired photon/neutral subflow `dN/dt=dX/dt=-kNX` with a stable `N-X` invariant, `D=0` limit, and symmetric Strang composition.\n- Real original Verner (1996) fitting coefficients from three pinned H I, He I, He II rows sourced through PR #152, preserving distinct photo-fit thresholds (13.60/24.59/54.42 eV) and binding energies.\n- Immutable source-resolved photon `q,mu_0` nodes in non-tilted LRS Bianchi I; angular photon Killing redshift/shear work, genuinely source-dependent opacity and positive He I \u2192 He II \u2192 He III species transitions.\n- Photon count, absorbed photon energy, ionization binding, photoheat and H/He nuclei ledgers. Absorbed z-momentum recorded, **baryon recoil Euler owner still OPEN**.\n- Equal source N=1 and Uq=60eV positive mono60 vs bimodal40/80 spectra show **different HeII events** by 0.0034146424031299347 per H. This is a conditional information-loss counterexample, not a novel global no-go.\n\n## Executed verification\n- CPython 3.13 ChatGPT isolated sandbox: original **22/22 unittest PASS**. Initial test assumption about transverse blueshift sign failed, preserved in archive, then corrected without changing source physics.\n- Independent SciPy DOP853 reference for coupled gas+photon ODE; 9-grid test, last four log-log slope **-1.9991920420775982**, final max state difference **3.7938619468214085e-8**. Largest tested number ledger residual 4.44e-16, energy ledger residual 4.26e-14 eV/H.\n- Wolfram symbolic exact pair ODE/IC/semigroup/D\u21920 checks **{0,0,0,0}**.\n- Published exact source bytes were fetched back through GitHub Git blobs: `source_aware.py` `db822a53da3ccdca7cf96628e9ef3bbcec83db5a`, `test_source_aware.py` `1253a47c6d09ec6361ef302cb1c829893bd8f823`, `run_study.py` `c352c9814234f7432e7ea50c47cf9fe56daa3320`, all equal to actually tested source files.\n\n## Durable archive and honest blockers\n- Source-restorable ZIP (including raw result arrays/logs/figure/manifest): `REI_SOURCE_AWARE_HE_PHOTO_REACTION_20261016_v1.zip`; 102560 bytes; SHA256 `52190fea5889be372a8baeb5b14c66b1d89563e6cb49cc397fcbc8b53df120e7`.\n- Uploaded to **owner-private Google Drive**: https://drive.google.com/file/d/10Uk7BBdF2MvqpxLlC9cdUiyGFuQpVX_U/view?usp=drivesdk; independently downloaded whole ZIP; exact SHA match; fresh extraction 22/22 PASS.\n- Dropbox upload **NOT COMPLETED**: Dropbox app's upload action requires fileParam injection unsupported by current tool path; mounted Dropbox Library is read-only. No false second-cloud receipt.\n- User workstation and 64-core NCP execution **NOT_RUN in this unit**: Desktop Commander monthly usage exhausted; running PR #150 full campaign untouched. Native subagent tool unavailable (NOT_RUN).\n- Physics ceiling: photoionization-only, prescribed geometry and nH; no recombination, collisional ionization, gas thermal evolution, source-age cosmological solver, full Einstein energy\u2013momentum closure, recoil coupling, reionization history or observational comparison.\n\n## Execution\n```bash\ncd research/rei_c16_photo_reaction_20261016\npython3 -m unittest -v test_source_aware.py\npython3 run_study.py\npython3 build_figure.py\n```\nPython, NumPy, SciPy, matplotlib. The archived result package is a stronger readback target than the branch alone.\n\nKeep this PR **DRAFT**, stacked on #149, not merged into production. Next scientific work requires exact PR150 native owner contract + source event histories and 3-species dynamic gas thermal/recombination ledger and error-controlled angular/spectral/time convergence.",
